<form class="form-horizontal hh-settings">
  <h4>Connection</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Klipper API socket</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xxlarge" data-bind="value: settings.settings.plugins.happyhare.socket_path"
             placeholder="auto (e.g. ~/printer_data/comms/klippy.sock)">
      <span class="help-block">
        Leave empty to detect it. Klipper must be started with <code>-a &lt;path&gt;</code> and OctoPrint
        must be able to read and write that socket. Current link:
        <strong data-bind="text: linkText"></strong>
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Print safety</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.settings.plugins.happyhare.protect_errors">
        Let Happy Hare handle MMU errors
      </label>
      <span class="help-block">
        Happy Hare reports an MMU problem as an <code>!!</code> line before it pauses, and OctoPrint
        treats that as a firmware error — which cancels the print or disconnects. With this on, the
        plugin swallows Happy Hare's own errors so the MMU can pause and you can recover. Klipper
        shutdowns, heater faults and MCU errors are never swallowed.
      </span>
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.settings.plugins.happyhare.render_prompts">
        Show Happy Hare's error dialog
      </label>
      <span class="help-block">
        Renders Klipper's <code>action:prompt_*</code> dialogs, which OctoPrint's own prompt support
        cannot display. RESUME and CANCEL are routed through OctoPrint so the job state stays in sync.
      </span>
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.settings.plugins.happyhare.print_end_on_cancel">
        Tell Happy Hare when a print is cancelled
      </label>
      <span class="help-block">
        Appends this to OctoPrint's <em>After print job is cancelled</em> script, otherwise Happy Hare
        never learns the job ended:
        <input type="text" class="input-large" data-bind="value: settings.settings.plugins.happyhare.cancel_command">
      </span>
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.settings.plugins.happyhare.strip_tool_temps">
        Strip the tool number from M104/M109
      </label>
      <span class="help-block">
        Klipper rejects <code>M104 T1 S…</code> on a single extruder machine with another
        <code>!!</code> line.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Uploads</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.settings.plugins.happyhare.preprocess_uploads">
        Substitute Happy Hare's slicer placeholders on upload
      </label>
      <span class="help-block">
        Does the job Happy Hare's Moonraker component does on a Mainsail machine:
        replaces <code>!referenced_tools!</code>, <code>!colors!</code>, <code>!temperatures!</code>,
        <code>!materials!</code>, <code>!purge_volumes!</code> and <code>!filament_names!</code>.
        Your slicer's start G-code has to call <code>MMU_START_SETUP</code> with those placeholders —
        copy this line:
      </span>
      <textarea rows="3" class="input-xxlarge" readonly data-bind="value: startGcodeSnippet"></textarea>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Interface</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Density</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <select data-bind="value: settings.settings.plugins.happyhare.density">
        <option value="auto">Auto (compact on narrow layouts and UI Customizer)</option>
        <option value="cozy">Always roomy</option>
        <option value="compact">Always compact</option>
      </select>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.settings.plugins.happyhare.confirm_moves">
        Confirm commands that move filament
      </label>
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.settings.plugins.happyhare.show_navbar">
        Show the MMU indicator in the top bar
      </label>
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.settings.plugins.happyhare.show_sensors">
        Show the sensor panel in the sidebar
      </label>
    </div>
  </div>
</form>
